document.write('<li class="rss-item"><a class="rss-item" href="http://www.guardian.co.uk/theguardian/2011/feb/08/archive-mafia-setback-alleged-leader-1964" target="_blank">From the archive, 8 February 1964: Mafia setback: alleged leader surrenders</a><br />');
document.write('<div class=\"track\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"http://hits.guardian.co.uk/b/ss/guardiangu-feeds/1/H.22.2/44033?ns=guardian&pageName=From+the+archive%2C+8+February+1964%3A+Mafia+setback%3A+alleged+leader+surrend%3AArticle%3A1516652&ch=From+the+Guardian&c3=Guardian&c4=Mafia+%28News%29%2CWorld+news%2CItaly+%28News%29&c5=Not+commercially+useful&c6=George+Armstrong&c7=11-Feb-08&c8=1516652&c9=Article&c10=&c11=From+the+Guardian&c13=From+the+archive+%28Guardian+series%29&c25=&c30=content&h2=GU%2FFrom+the+Guardian%2FMafia\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" /></div><p class=\"standfirst\">Originally published in the Guardian on 8 February 1964</p><p>VENICE, FEBRUARY 7</p><p>\"We are at a turning point. The Mafia no longer is feared and changes are in the wind. This is an historic moment.\" This is the comment of a Palermo magistrate to the surprising surrender and arrest of Giuseppe Genco Russo, the alleged Mafia chief. He turned himself in to the police of Caltanisetta, Sicily, shortly after midnight, saying: \"I hear you are looking for me. Here I am.\" Signor Russo, a strapping \"gentleman farmer\" of 71, had always been available for polite police questioning, or for press interviews, since the Mafia crown was supposedly passed to him in 1954, after the death, in his millionaire\'s bed, of the previous aged Mafia boss.</p><p>Signor Russo was in charge of the elaborate funeral and from that moment to now, he has been considered the most powerful man in Italy. Some days ago a Palermo Court, studying evidence which lately has come to light, decided that he could be charged with being \"dangerous to society.\" A warrant for his arrest was issued. The most powerful man in Sicily then became the least visible.</p><p>It is believed Signor Russo\'s two lawyers met quietly with the police earlier this week and agreed their client would surrender at an appointed hour.</p><p>He was assigned a \"special surveillance\" cell, which means two guards are on constant duty. On February 14 a magistrate will decide if Signor Russo is to be given the full penalty permitted by the law for those who officially may have committed no crimes but who are \"undesirable.\" This would mean the defendant could be sentenced to five years of obligatory residence in a distant part of Italy.</p><p>The Communists have made capital of Signor Russo\'s affiliation with the Christian Democratic Party over the years. (Under Fascism, the previous Mafia chief and Mussolini decided at a secret summit meeting to leave each other alone.) In 1960 he was elected to the city council of his Sicilian village on the Christian Democratic \"ticket.\" But neither his own organisation, nor the powerful Catholic Party, has been able to help him this time. Only a few years ago, most Sicilians were afraid to talk about the Mafia. Today, in Palermo, an art gallery is holding an anti-Mafia show of paintings by local artists depicting crimes attributed to the Mafia.</p><p><strong>George Armstrong</strong></p><p></p><p><em>[Giuseppe Russo was held before a special tribunal, accused of being \"socially undesirable\". On 24 February 1964 he was judged a social menace and sentenced to live in Lovere, in the Province of Bergamo, under police surveillance for five years.]</em></p><div class=\"related\" style=\"float: left; margin-right: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.guardian.co.uk/world/mafia\">Mafia</a></li><li><a href=\"http://www.guardian.co.uk/world/italy\">Italy</a></li></ul></div><br/><div class=\"terms\"><a href=\"http://www.guardian.co.uk\">guardian.co.uk</a> &copy; Guardian News & Media Limited 2011 | Use of this content is subject to our <a href=\"http://users.guardian.co.uk/help/article/0,,933909,00.html\">Terms & Conditions</a> | <a href=\"http://www.guardian.co.uk/help/feeds\">More Feeds</a></div><p style=\"clear:both\" /> <p><a href=\"http://feedads.g.doubleclick.net/~at/t9cLy2bZjEQPW2HYL07l4YAQ_Ao/0/da\"><img src=\"http://feedads.g.doubleclick.net/~at/t9c